//
// Path rendering prmitives
//
// Codes to handle line segment, arc, and quad bezier for path rendering.
// For each segment type, we calculate distance to the curve, winding number, and UV parameterization.
//
// The parametrization can be thought as local coordinate system, where U advances along the curve, and V across (zero on curve). 
//
// Each segment is defined by start and end point. For a closed curve to be filled, connected shapes should share exactly the same end points.
//
// Combining the winding numbers and distances from multiple shapes can be used to calculate signed distance to closed path,
// which can be used for filling, outline, shadows, etc.
//
// The winding number calculation works by calculating the area left of the end points, and then differencing the result with the actual curve shape.
// This calculation ensures that the part of the winding area that needs to be countered by other shapes is well controlled only by the end points.
// This allows us to carefully control the e.g. double counting the end points of a curve.
//
//
